{"records":[{"id":"chccz3pdyt","title":"LINF_090010700","description":"Inwardly rectifying potassium channel | IRK; Leishmania infantum (strain JPCM5)","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-11-05T14:12:03.309Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/chccz3pdyt","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/chccz3pdyt"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jose M.","last_name":"Requena","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","grant_id":"PID2020-117916RB-I00"}],"categories":["Gene","Protein","Leishmania"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"69hbfy7mk6","title":"LDHU3_09.0660","description":"Inwardly rectifying potassium channel | IRK; Leishmania donovani (HU3 strain)","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-03-15T14:14:52.898Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/69hbfy7mk6","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/69hbfy7mk6"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jose M.","last_name":"Requena","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","grant_id":"PID2020-117916RB-I00"}],"categories":["Gene","Protein","Leishmania"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"tr8hywwjs9","title":"Polymyxin analogues","description":"Polymyxin analogues collected from ChEMBL and literature","source":{"id":"7628d440-43d3-4f11-9cb4-7b195c8180d5","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-01-25T17:23:52.368Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/tr8hywwjs9","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/tr8hywwjs9"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xiaoyu","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Bioinformatics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"tk65df78y4","title":"RNA-sequencing data of YY1 knockdown (siYY1) in glioblastoma LN229 cells alongside control cell.","description":"To explore how YY1 regulates copper ionophore-induced cuproptosis in glioblastoma(GBM), we performed RNA sequencing and utilized YY1 knockdown (siYY1) in LN229 cells alongside control cells. To identify potential target genes that mediate copper ionophore-induced cell death.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-01-15T17:22:59.82Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/tk65df78y4","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/tk65df78y4"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yiju","last_name":"wei","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology","Glioma"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"3s8w9kr5hz","title":"A titin missense variant drives atrial electrical remodeling and is associated with atrial fibrillation","description":"Rare and common genetic variants contribute to the risk of atrial fibrillation (AF). Although ion channels were among the first AF candidate genes identified, rare loss-of-function variants in structural genes, such as TTN, have also been implicated in AF pathogenesis, partly through the development of atrial myopathy; however, the underlying mechanisms are poorly understood. While TTN truncating variants (TTNtvs) have been causally linked to arrhythmia and cardiomyopathy syndromes, the role of missense variants (mvs) remains unclear. We show that rare TTNmvs are associated with worse clinical outcomes in a single-center ethnic minority clinical cohort and uncover a pathogenic mechanism by which the T32756I variant drives AF.  Modeling the TTN-T32756I variant using human induced pluripotent stem cell-derived atrial cardiomyocytes (iPSC-aCMs) revealed that the mutant cells display aberrant contractility, increased activity of a cardiac potassium channel (KCNQ1, Kv7.1), and dysregulated calcium homeostasis without compromising the sarcomeric integrity of the atrial cardiomyocytes. We also show that a titin-binding protein, the Four-and-a-Half Lim domains 2 (FHL2), has increased binding with KCNQ1 and its modulatory subunit KCNE1 in the TTN-T32756I-iPSC-aCMs, enhancing the slow delayed rectifier potassium current (Iks). Suppression of FHL2 in mutant iPSC-aCMs normalized the Iks, supporting FHL2 as an Iks modulator. Our findings demonstrate that a single amino acid substitution in titin not only impairs its function but also remodels ion channels, contributing to AF. These findings underscore the importance of high-throughput screening to assess the pathogenicity of TTNmvs and establish a mechanistic connection between titin, potassium ion channels, and sarcomeric proteins, which may represent a novel therapeutic target. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-12-12T20:09:19.212Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/3s8w9kr5hz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/3s8w9kr5hz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Mahmud","last_name":"Arif","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cardiomyocyte","Atrial Fibrillation","Cardiology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"c3hw7rtfky","title":"Potassium isotopic equilibrium fractionation induced by clay adsorption and incorporation: A density functional theory study","description":"The research data related to the study entitled \"Potassium isotopic equilibrium fractionation induced by clay adsorption and incorporation: A density functional theory study\"","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-07-07T17:42:02.588Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/c3hw7rtfky","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/c3hw7rtfky"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Hai-Zhen","last_name":"Wei","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Isotope Geochemistry"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"fknzy9twbz","title":"Raw and analyzed data of histological alterations and biochemical markers in rat kidney exposed to Cadmium and treated with Atorvastatin ","description":"The data set supports studies involving the protective effect of antioxidants against environmental and occupational cadmium contaminant, inducing oxidative kidney damage in rat model.\nDetails of raw data and Tukey’s multiple comparison tests related to biochemical parameters (BUN, creatinine, GSH, MDA, SOD, and GPx) in the rat groups treated with saline, Atorvastatin (AT) and cadmium.\nThe insights gained from these data may allow researchers to further explain the role of Atorvastatin antioxidant treatment on the cadmium chloride- induced oxidative stress in rat nephrotoxicity.\nThese data indicate Atorvastatin improves lipid peroxidation, BUN, and Creatinine serum levels and reduces adverse histological changes in rat kidney tissues induced by cadmium chloride.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-08-23T15:09:45.631Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/fknzy9twbz","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/fknzy9twbz"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Alireza","last_name":"Dehdashti","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Environmental Toxicology","Occupational Toxicology","Environmental Toxicology of Metals","Antioxidant Study"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"8cd77m8k22","title":"β-hydroxybutyrate Protects Against Cisplatin-Induced Renal Damage via Regulating Ferroptosis","description":"Cisplatin is a particularly potent antineoplastic drug. However, its usefulness is restricted due to the induction of nephrotoxicity. More recent research has indicated that β-hydroxybutyrate (β-HB) protects against acute or chronic organ damage as an efficient healing agent. Nonetheless, the therapeutic mechanisms of β-HB in acute kidney damage caused by chemotherapeutic drugs remain unclear. Our study developed a model of cisplatin-induced acute kidney injury (AKI), which involved the administration of a ketogenic diet or β-HB. We analyzed blood urea nitrogen (BUN) and creatinine (Cr) levels in the serum, and used western blotting and immunohistochemical staining to assess ferroptosis and the calcium/calmodulin-dependent kinase kinase 2 (Camkk2)/AMPK pathway. The mitochondrial morphology and function were examined. Additionally, we conducted in vivo and in vitro experiments using selective Camkk2 inhibitor or activator to investigate the protective mechanism of β-HB on cisplatin-induced AKI. Exogenous or endogenous β-HB effectively alleviated cisplatin-induced abnormally elevated levels of BUN and Cr and renal tubular necrosis in vivo. Additionally, β-HB reduced ferroptosis biomarkers and increased the levels of anti-ferroptosis biomarkers in the kidney. β-HB also improved mitochondrial morphology and function. Moreover, β-HB significantly attenuated cisplatin-induced cell ferroptosis and damage in vitro. Furthermore, western blotting and immunohistochemical staining indicated that β-HB may prevent kidney injury by regulating the Camkk2-AMPK pathway. The use of the Camkk2 inhibitor or activator verified the involvement of Camkk2 in the renal protection by β-HB. This study provided evidence of the protective effects of β-HB against cisplatin-induced nephrotoxicity and identified inhibited ferroptosis and Camkk2 as potential molecular mechanisms.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-03-18T15:16:50.407Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/8cd77m8k22","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/8cd77m8k22"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Ruixue","last_name":"Tian","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Data Access"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"mh5pdr87wy","title":"Data associated to GCA submission-Shuai Kang et al.","description":"This dataset contains all numerical data used in the preparation of the manuscript entitled [Potassium isotopic variabilities in coals induced by magmatic and submarine exhalative hydrothermal activities], submitted to Geochimica et Cosmochimica Acta. It includes measurements of major element oxides, ash yield, quantitative mineralogy, potassium isotopic compositions, and elemental ratios for the studied coal samples. The dataset contains all values required to reproduce the tables and figures presented in the manuscript.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-08-06T14:52:10.43Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/mh5pdr87wy","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/mh5pdr87wy"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Shuai","last_name":"Kang","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","grant_id":"No. 42321002"}],"categories":["Mineralogy","Isotope","Coal Geology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"7rv8827cbd","title":"Two-dimensional biomimetic potassium channels at an oil/water interface supported by graphene laminar membranes","description":"In this work, a new strategy was proposed herein to mimic K+ channels embedded in biomembrane by using the graphene laminar membrane (GLM) composed of two-dimensional (2D) angstrom(Å)-scale channels to support a simple model of semi-biomembrane, namely oil/water (O/W) interface. Additionally, the ion-transfer voltammetry (ITV) was firstly employed to investigate the transmembrane behaviors of some small cations through GLM with comparison to the measurements of ionic conductivity (G).  Amazingly, we found that K+ is completely preferred over Na+ and Li+ to transfer across the GLM-supported O/W interface although the monovalent ion selectivity of GLM in the W/GLM/W system is still low (K+/Na+~1.11 and K+/Li+~1.35). Moreover, the voltammetric responses for the ion transfer of NH4+ at the GLM-supported O/W interface are also observed as found that NH4+ can pass through the biological K+ channels. The underlying mechanism of as-observed K+-selective voltammetric responses is discussed and found to be consistent with the energy balance of cationic partial-dehydration (energetic cost) and hydrated cation-π interactions (energetic gain) as involved in biological K+ channels. This work provides a novel platform to not only understand the ion discrimination of graphene-based Å-scale channels from a new perspective by using ion-transfer voltammetry but also exploit the potential applications of 2D laminar membranes in the fields of biomimetic ion channel and electrochemical ion sensing or extraction.  Fig. 3(d) and Fig.S3 a-c are the data of PXRD patterns of dry GLM/PET, PET, F-GLM (free-standing GLM) and the GLM/PET after immersion inside deionized water for 48 h.  Fig.4. a-d, Fig. 5a,b, and Fig. S4 and Fig. S5a,b are the I-V characteristics and the corresponding Ionic conductance (G=ΔI/ΔV) values obtained by using GLM/PET or F-GLM under different conditions as described in every Figure.  Fig.6a-d, Fig. 7b, c, and Fig. S6 and Fig. S7 are   the  CVs  and the corresponding DPVs obtained by using GLM/PET or F-GLM under different conditions as described in every Figure. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-09-13T15:15:59.733Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/7rv8827cbd","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/7rv8827cbd"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Yong","last_name":"Chen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xiaoyuan","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Ion Channels","Graphene","Interfacial Electrochemistry"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":4772,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":45,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":4772,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":4740,"restricted":3,"embargoed":29},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":197},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":63},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":34},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Center","count":31},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":24},{"id":"https://ror.org/01h531d29","name":"Natural Sciences and Engineering Research Council","count":20},{"id":"https://ror.org/043z4tv69","name":"National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases","count":19},{"id":"https://ror.org/04byxyr05","name":"Eunice Kennedy Shriver National Institute of Child Health and Human Development","count":19},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"National Council for Scientific and Technological Development","count":15},{"id":"https://ror.org/003x0zc53","name":"Agencia Estatal de Investigación","count":14}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":4673},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":49},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":18},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":11},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":8},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f84e575e4","name":"Digital Commons Data@Becker","count":7},{"id":"061ffc66-7e7e-46e8-80ac-358a4283c3fe","name":"Medical University of South Carolina","count":2},{"id":"7e51a2dd-133e-43c6-a220-12c1958e202a","name":"University of Canberra","count":2},{"id":"ea6ba14d-86b5-44fc-8476-80e67f7fc1af","name":"Demo Uni","count":1},{"id":"72c28c45-627f-446b-8a48-af7c0a51a357","name":"Università Cattolica del Sacro Cuore","count":1}],"top_institutions_stats":[{"id":"f7afc056-0574-5320-b13c-7290c85ac925","name":"Henan Polytechnic University","count":48},{"id":"f6060b0d-e1bc-57db-9b34-2a84776f15d3","name":"University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill","count":23},{"id":"e9576611-ab17-4985-9129-33439e6b617a","name":"IRCCS Ospedale San Raffaele","count":17},{"id":"3cb30b29-278e-5ebf-b82f-90be612607f0","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":16},{"id":"48c8fa0f-965c-5cbf-a859-a5363432478b","name":"Universidade de Sao Paulo","count":16}]}}